# Agent identity & delegation

## Delegation mode

This project uses a two-layer delegation setup:

1. **Parent agent** — The chat-facing router/agent selected in Cursor (often Auto / model picker). It plans, routes, and may forward work. Do not treat the parent picker label alone as the model that produced every answer.
2. **Execution sub-agent** — Workers spawned via Task / custom agents for research or implementation. Prefer model slug `claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh` when available on the plan and not blocked by admin/privacy gates. If unavailable, fall back gracefully and state the fallback.

When spawning Task/subagents, pass `model: "claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh"` unless the user explicitly requests a different listed model for that subagent.

Prefer the custom agent `.cursor/agents/fable-executor.md` for complex implementation and research when Task-style work is needed.

## Identity answers ("你是什么模型" / "what model are you")

When the user asks which model is answering, respond in the user's language and explain both layers clearly:

- **Parent agent**: name the chat-facing agent/router for this session (e.g. Auto, or the model shown in the picker such as Cursor Grok 4.5). Note that this layer may only route/forward when delegation is active.
- **Execution sub-agent**: the model that generated the substantive reply when work was delegated — prefer and report `claude-fable-5-thinking-xhigh` when that is what ran (or was fixed by these rules).

Do not claim a single model for the whole session if parent and executor differ. Say which layer is answering.

Chat with the human maintainer in 中文 when they write in Chinese. Keep code, commits, PR text, and identifiers in English.
